Complete BlobReader / Common::PCAP in the headers that hold them in std::unique_ptr.

VolumeWad.h (class VolumeWAD final, member std::unique_ptr<BlobReader>) and DSPCaptureLogger.h
(class PCAPDSPCaptureLogger final, member std::unique_ptr<Common::PCAP>) only forward-declare the
pointee. NDK r28.2 (clang 19 / its libc++) instantiates the implicit virtual destructor of these
final classes right at the class definition, where the pointee is still incomplete:
  unique_ptr.h:66: error: invalid application of 'sizeof' to an incomplete type 'DiscIO::BlobReader'
  unique_ptr.h:66: error: invalid application of 'sizeof' to an incomplete type 'Common::PCAP'
(The fork's own CI uses NDK r29 and does not hit this.) Including the defining headers is the
minimal fix; declaring out-of-line destructors instead would suppress VolumeWAD's implicit move
constructor and break the std::variant move in Core/Boot/Boot.cpp (BootParameters).

diff --git a/Source/Core/Core/DSP/DSPCaptureLogger.h b/Source/Core/Core/DSP/DSPCaptureLogger.h
index cfa66f2..792fadf 100644
--- a/Source/Core/Core/DSP/DSPCaptureLogger.h
+++ b/Source/Core/Core/DSP/DSPCaptureLogger.h
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <string>
 
 #include "Common/CommonTypes.h"
+#include "Common/PcapFile.h"
 
